<title>MOROCCO: Moroccan Treasury auction raised 154.5 mln dirhams.</title>
<headline>Moroccan Treasury auction raised 154.5 mln dirhams.</headline>
<dateline>RABAT 1996-11-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Moroccan Treasury raised 154.5 million dirhams from a treasury bill auction earlier this week, Bank al-Maghrib (central bank) said.</p>
<p>The auction took place on November 12, and the maturity date set to November 19, 1996, the bank said on Thursday.</p>
<p>Rates were unchanged and bids in million dirhams were as follows:</p>
<p>    MATURITY	BID	  AMOUNT	    INTEREST RATE</p>
<p>    26 weeks	52	   not allocated     8.5 percent</p>
<p>    52 weeks	10.25	not allocated     9.0  percent</p>
<p>    10 years	90	   90		   10.25 percent</p>
<p>    15 years	64.5	 64.5		 10.50 percent</p>
<p>----------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>    Total	   154.5	154.5</p>
<p>The Treasury raised in a previous auction 339.75 million dirhams. The auction took place on October 29, and the maturity was set to November 4, 1996, the bank said.</p>
<p>($1= 8.6 dirhams)</p>
<p>- Rabat newsroom +212-7 726518</p>
